00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:13.130
is if we just and everything I'm gonna say

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:17.030
I'm gonna assume kind of a
really simple classical physics

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:19.640
picture of the world but
nothing really hinges on that.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.900
It just kind of makes
it a little bit simpler.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.720
So if you think of a box of gas

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.320
with a bunch of particles bouncing around,

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:30.157
you can sort of
mathematically represent that

00:05:30.157 --> 00:05:32.690
if there's end particles bouncing around

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:37.430
and each particle has three
numbers that pick up position

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:39.850
and three numbers that pick out velocity,

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:42.130
then a six to the end dimensional space

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:46.360
kind of one point in that
completely describes right.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.350
Completely described that system.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.930
And what it is to say
that the laws of physics

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.740
are time symmetric,

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.730
is to say that what the laws really do,

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:59.950
is they pick out allowable
path through that space space.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.443
And to say that they're time symmetric,

00:06:01.443 --> 00:06:03.160
it's just to say that,

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:06.273
any time the laws allow
a path going this way,

00:06:06.273 --> 00:06:10.413
they allow the fact same pathway
in the opposite direction.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.240
There's some slight infelicities in that

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:15.260
but none that really matter, right?

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:19.710
Okay, so, as Carlo pointed out,

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.600
